<title>USA: Park-Ohio Q3 shr with gain rises to $1.00.</title>
<headline>Park-Ohio Q3 shr with gain rises to $1.00.</headline>
<dateline>CLEVELAND 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>(in thousands, except per share data)</p>
<p>			    3 mos ended Sept 30  9 mos ended Sept 30</p>
<p>					 1996    1995     1996     1995</p>
<p> Net sales			$79,750 $77,164 $261,297 $207,806</p>
<p> Gross profit		    13,044  11,548   44,004   34,702</p>
<p> Oper Income			2,113   2,059    7,245    8,976</p>
<p> Discontinued operations, net 8,817     956   11,642    2,600</p>
<p> Net income			10,930   3,015   18,887   11,576</p>
<p> Continuing operations per shr 0.19    0.12     0.66     0.59</p>
<p> Discontinued operations	 0.81    0.06     1.06     0.17</p>
<p> Net income			  1.00    0.18     1.72     0.76</p>
<p>Net income:</p>
<p> Continuing operations	   0.19    0.19     0.66     0.89</p>
<p> Discontinued operations	 0.81    0.09     1.06     0.26</p>
<p> Net income			  1.00    0.28     1.72     1.15</p>
<p> Average shares		  10,924  10,798   10,977   10,040</p>
<p>NOTES: Third quarter 1996 includes income of $8.5 million or $0.79 per share from the gain on the sale of Bennett Industries Inc subsidiary on July 31.</p>
<p>Data includes March 1995 purcahse of all shares of RB&amp;W Corp in exchange for 2.023 million Park-Ohio common shares.</p>
